FFmpeg 7.1.2 for Onyx -- https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-7.1.2.tar.xz, unchanged (tests/ref left out: the
FATE suite's reference outputs) but for one Onyx patch: libavutil/aarch64/timer.h reads cntvct_el0 with
-D__ONYX__ (build.sh pi), not the PMU's pmccntr_el0 -- the apps run at EL0, where the PMU is closed
(av_get_random_seed, reached by a subtitle's colour "random", killed the Media Player). The committed
libavutil.a got that one member, random_seed.o, rebuilt (ar rD) -- the rest is as build.sh made it.

Used by Onyx's media library, user/av (av_ffmpeg.c: libavcodec's decoders; av_lavf.c: libavformat's
demuxers), when compiled with -DAV_WITH_FFMPEG: the Media Player (user/Makefile's media.elf).

Licence: built with --enable-gpl, FFmpeg is GPL-2.0-or-later (COPYING.GPLv2, LICENSE.md); every program
linking it is distributed under the GPL-2.0 (the Media Player: docs/LICENSING.md).

Build: onyx/build.sh (pi: onyx/aarch64/*.a, committed; host: the PC's, for the simulator and the tests).
The headers in onyx/include are make install-headers' (avconfig.h: little-endian, fast unaligned -- the
same on the Pi and the PC).
